# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MOASYS-Vault — Shows ignore list (EXAMPLE)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# A "do not warn me about this" list for your shows library. Anything you put
# here gets silently dropped from output/<drive>/shows/warnings.json on every
# run.
#
# Ignore lists are per DRIVE as well as per type, because the paths below are
# relative to that drive's root_path. `<drive>` is the lowercased `name` of a
# root in config.json — e.g. `server`, `external`.
#
# How to use this file:
#   1. Copy this file to `ignored/<drive>/shows.yaml` (create the drive
#      folder, drop the `.example` suffix). The real per-drive files are
#      gitignored so your personal decisions don't end up in version control.
#   2. Add path prefixes below — one per line.
#   3. Re-run `npm run shows <drive>`. Matching warnings disappear from the
#      output.
#
# Two entry shapes — pick whichever fits each case:
#
#   # 1. Path-only (a bare string) — silences EVERY warning under this path.
#   - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
#
#   # 2. Type-scoped (an object) — silences only the listed warning types
#   #    under this path. Other warnings on the same path stay visible.
#   - path: HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
#     types:
#       - warn_episode_gaps
#       - warn_tmdb_episode_count
#
# Matching is case-insensitive and forward-slash-normalized, so the same
# file works on Windows (backslashes) and macOS/Linux (forward slashes).
#
# Get the paths to add from output/<drive>/shows/warnings.json and
# output/<drive>/shows/validation-warnings.json — paths live under each `by_type`
# bucket. The bucket key (e.g. `warn_episode_gaps`) is the warning type;
# you can also find every type listed in rules/shows.yaml under `checks`.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────


# Silence a whole show you can't fix
# (Use this when a show has known missing episodes — never released on disc,
# culled by the rights holder, etc. — and you don't want to see
# warn_episode_gaps / warn_tmdb_episode_count noise every run.)
# - HD/Channel 4 Catchup (2024)
# - HD/Some Reality Show (2020)


# Silence one season
# (The rest of the show's warnings stay live, but everything under this
# specific season folder is dropped.)
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
# - UHD/Star Trek Enterprise (2001)/Season 4


# Silence one episode
# (Pin-point: just one file. Useful when one episode has a legitimate quality
# outlier you've decided to accept.)
# - HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 1/Some Show (2020) - S01E05.mp4


# Silence a whole category folder
# (Drops EVERY warning under this folder.)
# - Other HD
# - Other SD


# Silence one warning type for a specific path
# (Most precise option. The example below silences ONLY the episode-gap
# warnings for that season — everything else under it stays visible.)
# - path: HD/Some Show (2020)/Season 2
#   types:
#     - warn_episode_gaps
#     - warn_tmdb_episode_count
